          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, that is the point of a 120V compact dryer. Plug it directly into a grounded wall outlet, never into an extension cord or power strip, and keep other heavy loads off that circuit while it runs. Many manuals call for a dedicated circuit, often 20A. Check the nameplate and manual, and have a licensed electrician add a circuit if needed."
