          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it safe to use a portable dryer without a vent?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not a standard vented dryer. Without a vent, the moisture and fine lint go into your living space, causing mold and damp walls. Use an indoor exhaust option only if your manual explicitly permits it, and run a dehumidifier if you do. A true ventless condenser or heat pump dryer is designed to run without a vent, or use a spin dryer and a rack."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a portable dryer take to dry a load?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Longer than a full-size dryer, because a 120V heater is much smaller. Drying time depends mostly on how wet the clothes are, the fabric and the load size, so manufacturers rarely publish firm times. Owners commonly report that loads from small portable washers can take well over an hour. Spinning clothes harder before drying is the most effective way to shorten it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is a ventless dryer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A ventless dryer removes moisture from the exhaust inside the machine instead of blowing it outdoors. Condenser dryers cool the air and collect water in a tank or drain line; heat pump dryers do the same more efficiently. They are designed to run without an outdoor vent. A vented dryer with an indoor lint bag is not a ventless dryer, because the moisture still enters the room."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I stack a portable dryer on a portable washer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only with a matching front-load compact washer and the manufacturer's stacking kit for those exact models. Never stack a dryer on a top-loading portable washer, whose lid has to open and whose cabinet is not built to carry weight. Some compact dryers can be wall-mounted with a manufacturer kit, which must be fastened into studs or solid blocking."
          }
